                        


SCP-5487 

Containment Class:  Safe

Special Containment Procedures:  The underground complex SCP-5487 occupies has been repurposed and designated Provisional Site-405. MTF unit Iota-27 (“Art Connoisseurs”) has been created to explore the different SCP-5487-1s generated by SCP-5487. Site-405 is to be staffed by no less than 3 security personnel, and 2 research personnel at all times.

Description:  SCP-5487 is located in █████, United States. SCP-5487 resembles a Dell Dimension 4500, but it has 2 extra oddly shaped ports at the back. The first of these ports is connected by wire to a mahogany door frame, although no door is present within the frame. The second is connected to what appears to be a large scanner, about 2ft x 2ft.

When powered on, SCP-5487 will display an interface if a monitor is connected. The interface includes variables, parameters, and measurements, as well as a button labeled as “Start” and a faded button labeled as “Stop”. When a painting is inserted into the scanner and “Start” is pressed, the doorframe will create a portal into a computer generated replica of the painting present within the scanner, hereby referred to as SCP-5487-1.

When entered, the subject will be placed in front of the focal point of the painting, and an identical mahogany door will appear behind them. The space appears 3D, and subjects can walk into the foreground and background, as well as behind objects or off the side of what is present in the painting. There appears to be no limit to how expansive SCP-5487-1 is.

If humans or other creatures are on the painting, they appear in SCP-5487-1 and are capable of self locomotion. Humans are capable of speaking and conscious thought. These creatures will be doing the task that they appear to be doing in the painting when the subject enters SCP-5487-1.

