MTF Unit:  Iota-27 (“Art Connoisseurs”)

MTF Squad:  Delta-2

SCP-5487-1:  Melancholy Tunes on a Flemish Winter’s Day by Jos de Mey

Task:  Discover any deviations from baseline reality.

Foreword:  Due to a malfunction in the recording equipment, audio was not properly stored, and could not be recovered.

 

0:00: Lt. Gibson, Sgt. Grant, Pvt. Jones and Pvt. Williams exit the door in front of the middle pillar in the painting. The man sitting on the sidewalk playing the bagpipes looks questioningly at them, but continues playing.

0:01: The group moves into the foreground of the painting, which appears to be a city square. No abnormalities other than what is present in the original painting are immediately noticeable.

0:08: Lt. Gibson instructs Sgt. Grant and Pvt. Jones to investigate the street layout. When the group splits, Lt. Gibson and Pvt. Williams begin attempting to question the locals. However, everyone they attempt to speak to glances around and then briskly walks away.

0:19: Sgt. Grant takes his 9th right turn, and has yet to cross back across his path. Pvt. Jones, however, took 8 left turns and, without crossing his own path, saw Sgt. Grant down the same street.

0:22: Sgt. Grant and Pvt. Jones meet up and begin heading back.

0:25: Pvt. Williams has found a resident that appears to be willing to speak, although lip reading software is unable to determine what it is saying.

0:37: The group meets up again and heads back into the door, ending the exploration.

 





